# cipher — environment
#
# Copy to .env.local and fill in. .env.local is gitignored; this file is not,
# so NEVER put a real value here.
#
#   cp apps/web/.env.example apps/web/.env.local
#
# Restart the dev server after changing any of these. NEXT_PUBLIC_ values are
# inlined at BUILD time, so an edit while the server is running does nothing
# and looks exactly like a wrong value.


# ── Privy: login and embedded wallets ────────────────────────────────────────
#
# From dashboard.privy.io → your app → Settings → Basics.
#
# The APP ID is public by design. It ships to the browser in every page, which
# is what the NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix means. It is not a secret and never was.
#
# The APP SECRET is a real secret. It stays server-side and is used only by
# lib/auth/session.ts to verify the access token on gated API routes. Anyone
# holding it can mint sessions as any of your users.
NEXT_PUBLIC_PRIVY_APP_ID=
PRIVY_APP_SECRET=


# ── The model fallback ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# From console.anthropic.com. Server-side only — it is read by
# app/api/compile/route.ts and never reaches the browser.
#
# OPTIONAL. Without it cipher runs entirely on the deterministic grammar, which
# covers the sentences people actually type; the long tail comes back as a
# refusal that says so. With it, "dump half my bags if it craps out" compiles.
#
# The model never touches execution. It fills a closed schema, that schema is
# re-validated twice, and anything that moves money still goes through
# validate.ts and a readback the user approves.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Which model compiles sentences. Defaults to claude-opus-5.
# claude-haiku-4-5 is a fifth of the input cost and is well suited to a small
# structured extraction like this — a spending decision, so it lives here.
CIPHER_COMPILE_MODEL=


# ── Solana data ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Not needed yet. The chart, the market list and the depth reading all come
# from Binance, which is keyless — see lib/market/binance.ts.
#
# These land with the Solana leg: Helius for RPC and websockets, Birdeye for
# pool-level prices and metadata.
HELIUS_API_KEY=
BIRDEYE_API_KEY=
